At global sizes 3.0/2.2/1.7/1.4 mm, 23,136/44,194/88,065/150,681 nodes, VM was 18.311/18.457/17.841/18.334 MPa and Z tension 15.920/15.067/15.849/16.117 MPa. The 2.2 mm washer-supported case gave VM 18.397 and Z tension 15.240 MPa, compared with 18.457 and 15.067 for hole walls at the same size. The reaction was −150 N X within 0.01 N; deflection was 2.832–2.849 mm for hole walls and 3.043 mm for washers. The 61 MPa washer-edge stress in the different reinforced variant is a support idealization, not a governing material stress.

To resolve local variation, with global 3 mm and hole-wall controls 1.0/0.8/0.6 mm, nodes were 25,889/29,633/38,052, VM 18.233/18.974/19.270 MPa, Z tension 16.206/16.081/16.313 MPa and Z shear 6.914/6.807/6.888 MPa. All three change under 5% in the last step. The last local Z tension gives **22.5/16.313 = 1.38**, below the requested 2; the higher load-region VM gives **45/19.270 = 2.34**. Verdict **fail**. The loaded hole region is retained in these maxima; only the 6 mm fixture exclusion is applied. The rigid bore and rigid hole load cases are reported above as additional sensitivity checks.

## T4 — sharp corner'"''')
