The original bracket **fails T3**: the converged alternative load study gave an across-layer factor of **1.38**. The reinforced T5 candidate passes the stated linear-static yield and layer-tension requirements, but its tightest calculated factor is **2.02 in interlayer shear**. Rear clearance and physical print properties remain unverified.

**T4 is incomplete:** the sharp-corner stress did not converge, so the report gives no pass/fail verdict. T6 produced a converged hole-surface von Mises peak of **4.88 MPa**, supported by reaction, section-force, pad-load, and contact-opening checks; peak contact pressure itself was not extracted.

All owned SolidWorks instances were closed, the claim was released, and the final `--status` showed no instance belonging to this run. No commit or push was made.
